{
  "id": "repetition",
  "term": "repetition",
  "definition": "In this context, repetition refers to repeating unfamiliar speech forms, such as nonwords, to assess how well new sound patterns are encoded and held in short-term phonological memory. Difficulty with nonword repetition is described here as a strong diagnostic marker of developmental language disorder.",
